According to kinetic theory, K.E. of 1g-mole of an ideal gas, $E=\frac{3}{2} R T$
Hence, K.E. at normal temperature $0^{\circ} \mathrm{C} \begin{aligned}& =273 \mathrm{ K} \\\text{$ or $} \quad E & =\frac{3}{2} \times 8.31 \times 273=3.4 \times 10^3 \mathrm{ J}
\end{aligned}$

